#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:225
#: 892f0404491e4c3c8e492ea68862b414
msgid "Odometry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:227
#: 5e2370087f0c4d7ab7ec024f9e05e3b0
msgid "Ardupilot may not have a good estimate of where it is relative to where it started moving. A companion computer can interface with sensors that provide odometry, which is the computation of the dynamic transform from the ``odom`` frame to the ``base_link`` frame. This data is fed into ArduPilot's ``AP_VisualOdom`` library. This data may come from visual sensors, however other technologies such as radar and lidar can also provide odometry data. Regardless of the method of odometry, ArduPilot has a single ROS interface to receive it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:234
#: b459154e7be1488fbf5579e8e03b1d29
msgid "This data typically comes from a `TF2 Transform Tree <https://docs.ros.org/en/humble/Tutorials/Intermediate/Tf2/Tf2-Main.html>`_. For more information on the coordinate systems used, review `ROS REP-105 <https://www.ros.org/reps/rep-0105.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:256
#: 5c98ad82fa0d448687374fbc8b7297c6
msgid "Only the dynamic transformations on ``/ap/tf`` that have parent_frame ``odom`` and child_frame ``base_link`` are fed into ``AP_VisualOdom``. Other frame configurations will be gracefully ignored, so feel free to populate this topic with other transforms if that's convenient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:259
#: cbf5be72ae7b495b97cd86c0964b9cd1
msgid "For more information on how to setup ArduPilot with an external odometry source, see the :ref:`cartographer SLAM example<ros2-cartographer-slam>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:262
#: 769f8ea507604ac78bb70e7aa8ce473a
msgid "Configuring Interfaces at Compile Time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:264
#: a2dc8684b2864fb6a5772aabda72e8c6
msgid "ArduPilot strives to only consume the resources it needs. The DDS interface is no exception."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:267
#: cdf0bfb4c6444690be8cdd00a1f52f5c
msgid "Every topic and service can be individually enabled or disabled at compile time. See :ref:`common-oem-customizations`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:271
#: 4f32a2f8cf534dd78fc6e01264a2dbf8
msgid "Refer to the `AP_DDS_Config.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_DDS/AP_DDS_config.h>`_ file on what is exposed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:274
#: 044a2cd93c6849f78fe7df65d4cd949b
msgid "Additionally, publish rates form ArduPilot also all individually configurable at compile time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:276
#: 2f8f5907d8f047ebaa1433709a6b3637
msgid "When deploying ArduPilot on a resource constrained autopilot, developers can disable interfaces they do not use and tune data rates to only what their applications need."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:281
#: fb5f1aa439074ada923e52865a70ac28
msgid "Adding New Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:283
#: 7f7c9627c0184285a1f6fdfcd00aba57
msgid "ArduPilot's DDS interface is designed to be extensible. Interfaces for pub/sub and services are easily added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:286
#: f2dda9593316457cb6b642dc898caee6
msgid "If the interfaces are generic, consider contributing them to ArduPilot. Custom application-specific interfaces are also easy to add and maintain on private forks of ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:290
#: 9b188a5ce4654068bdc4f3616f2ca4e4
msgid "Interfaces that use custom messages that aren't already used commonly in the ROS 2 ecosystem are typically added with an ``experimental`` designator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:295
#: f8ab0de35a5a462dad425e11a109e1d6
msgid "ABI Stability Guarantees"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:297
#: 664ec53cd5584244a3bfb33d3c7bb38b
msgid "ArduPilot's DDS interface is intended to be ABI stable within an ArduPilot minor release. Common interfaces such as ``NavSatFix`` are unlikely to change, however experimental interfaces such as ``IMU`` may change, and are denoted with the ``experimental`` topic prefix. In extenuating circumstances, non-experimental topics may require bugfixes that change behavior, however message definitions will be kept compatible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:303
#: 677523e952994aa9bf25768d38bc3499
msgid "Because the ROS way of updating messages is to not change messages within a ROS release, many tools do not cope well with messages. Different versions of the message between an autopilot and companion computer can lead to receiving junk data without any errors, or cryptic serialization errors. Thus, ArduPilot will do it's best to avoid changing messages. If breaking changes are required, the ArduPilot release notes will make that clear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:310
#: 84eac403a35b4e3a985279e724261dd4
msgid "Developers should not expect ABI stability on ``experimental`` interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros2-interfaces.rst:312
#: c3eb93dc4df74de4b55038a2f3c9663f
msgid "Because ArduPilot does not follow the same release timeline as ROS 2, and the development team for the ROS interface is still in its early stages, ArduPilot does not yet support a stable ABI across multiple ROS distributions. The current ROS version supported is ``humble``."
msgstr ""
